    "updated_at": "2023-04-17T21:24:38Z",
    "body": "> It feels like hiding a showing popover should end with it being in the hidden state.\r\n\r\nRight - I agree with this, and I think it's what already happens. Since removing the popover already hides it. It shouldn't be possible to move an open popover to a new document and have that new document's popover stack get affected by that node move. If I'm wrong, we should fix that.\r\n\r\nSide note, in the OP, I think `(e.newState == \"closed\")` should maybe be `(e.newState == \"open\")`, based on the text there?",
